{"event": "report", "t": 1795254416.586, "claim": "fixed", "text": "ter`, DuckDB, `schema: analytics`), and `models/sources.yml` declaring `ANALYTICS.FACT_MARKETING_SPEND`.\n- `models/marts/marketing/rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed.sql`, which:\n  - collapses all channels to one row per campaign per day,\n  - keeps the single channel with the highest total spend per campaign (ties go to the lowest key),\n  - sets `cohort_date` to the first spend date and computes `days_since_cohort`,\n  - computes running totals from unrounded sums and rounds only at the output, so the final row reconciles exactly.\n\n**Verification**\n- `dbt run` succeeded (1 model, PASS=1).\n- Output has 994 rows across 30 campaigns. That is 1000 source rows minus 6 duplicate campaign-day pairs that were collapsed.\n- Column types match the spec.\n- No duplicate `(campaign_id, days_since_cohort)` pairs.\n- No negative values.\n- Cumulative spend and revenue are non-decreasing within each campaign.\n- Each campaign has one `channel_key`.\n- For all 30 campaigns, the last row's cumulative totals match source totals exactly (max difference 0.0000).\n- `is_paid_back` is consistent with `cumulative_revenue >= cumulative_spend` on every row.\n\n**Choices and deviations you should know about**\n- `payback_ratio` is `cumulative_revenue / cumulative_spend`, rounded to 4 decimals, and is null-safe.\n- `is_paid_back` is evaluated per row, so a campaign can flip back to false when later spend outpaces revenue. I followed the spec literally; if you want it to latch once paid back, that is a small change.\n- The spec names `/app/dbt_transforms`, but that path does not exist. The reference project is `/app/dbt_models_duckdb`, and I used its DuckDB setup as the reference.\n- `DB_TYPE=duckdb`, so I wrote only the DuckDB profile. I did not write a Snowflake output.\n- The model does not use `dbt_utils`, so no package install was needed.\n- The `main.FACT_MARKETING_SPEND` copy is identical in row count and spend total, so I used the `ANALYTICS` table that the rest of the project references.\n\nVERDICT: fixed", "verdict": null}
